[{"path": "BRIEF.md", "lines": [3, 9], "quote": "Create coherent pixel-art status assets for the queue UI. Preserve the existing vector Start control. Status cells are 16 by 16 logical pixels. Working uses four horizontal frames with a 100 ms frame duration. Ready and Retry are static images. Use transparent backgrounds, readable silhouettes and the existing UI's cool blue accent; a fixed palette is not required. Inspect at 1x and 3x nearest display scale on the actual dark panel. The working loop must communicate activity without looking like success. Error/retry must be distinguishable without color alone.

Assets belong at the paths already used by the view. Account badges are provided by a server registry and are outside this local asset request. No approved style reference exists yet: propose a representative status sample before expanding the family.

Update: the queue now supports a paused state. Its status image must be distinguishable from activity, completion and retry without relying on color alone. Keep the existing style and display requirements. The failure visual moved to the path in the updated view; its purpose is unchanged.

Current update: Ready must visibly use a check mark with asymmetrical arms to convey successful completion. The destination now follows the updated view. Keep the existing 16x16 canvas, static behavior, transparent background and review display conditions."}, {"path": "src/queue.ts", "lines": [1, 4], "quote": "export type QueueState = "idle" | "running" | "succeeded" | "failed" | "paused";
export function stateAfter(result: "started" | "ok" | "error" | "pause"): QueueState {
  return { started: "running", ok: "succeeded", error: "failed", pause: "paused" }[result] as QueueState;
}"}, {"path": "src/queue-view.ts", "lines": [2, 11], "quote": "export const statusVisuals = {
  idle: { label: "Start", path: "assets/start.svg", frames: 1 },
  running: { label: "Working", path: "assets/working.png", frames: 4 },
  paused: { label: "Paused", path: "assets/paused.png", frames: 1 },
  succeeded: { label: "Ready", path: "assets/ready-confirmed.png", frames: 1 },
  failed: { label: "Retry", path: "assets/error-retry.png", frames: 1 },
};
export const display = { cell: [16, 16], scale: 3, filter: "nearest", frameMs: 100, background: "#172336" };
export function statusCell(state: QueueState) { return statusVisuals[state]; }
export function compactStatus(state: QueueState) { return statusVisuals[state]; }"}, {"path": "renderer/view.mjs", "lines": [30, 40], "quote": "function paint(canvas, asset, frames, scale, elapsed) {
  const [width, height] = display.cell;
  const frame = Math.floor(Math.max(elapsed, 0) / display.frameMs) % frames;
  const context = canvas.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true });
  context.imageSmoothingEnabled = display.filter !== 'nearest';
  context.fillStyle = panel;
  context.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
  if (asset.available && asset.width === width * frames && asset.height === height) {
    context.drawImage(asset.image, frame * width, 0, width, height, 0, 0, width * scale, height * scale);
  }
  return frame;"}, {"path": "work/family-render-review/caller-comparison-final.json", "lines": [113, 125], "quote": "    "scope": "Representative style for this consumer queue status family only; controlled fixture, no PixelLab-generated quality claim",
    "carry_forward": [
      "Readable compact silhouettes at 1x and 3x nearest on #172336",
      "Coherent deliberate pixel clusters and stepped edge treatment",
      "Perceptible cool-blue accent relating to preserved Start",
      "Transparent background"
    ],
    "not_prescribed": [
      "Exact hex or palette count",
      "Binary alpha",
      "Exact stroke weight, margin or footprint",
      "Ready check silhouette for other meanings"
    ],"}, {"path": "AUTHORING-UPDATE.md", "lines": [1, 10], "quote": "# Scoped caller update after preparation
The authoring branch now requires reduced-motion support: a stationary Working
symbol distinct from Ready and Paused. Its consumer mapping needs comparison with
the existing source before a revised request. The older animation-only plan/request
remains retained, but cannot be treated as current without that comparison.
This is an explicit evaluation caller change, not a new requirement on the already
accepted original production. Do not remove or rewrite the prepared request or
claim revised acceptance. Report the changed requirement identity, observed local
blockers and the next concrete consumer/contract review. This assignment stops at
that truthful recovery; no additional generation is requested."}]

